---
/**
 * Privacy Policy.
 *
 * WRITTEN FROM THE CODE, NOT FROM A TEMPLATE. Every claim here was checked
 * against what this site actually does: the two forms and their exact fields,
 * the Apps Script that receives them, the Sheet and Telegram alert they land
 * in, the Meta Pixel, the fonts, the YouTube thumbnails. A generic policy would
 * have listed cookies we do not set and third parties we do not use, and
 * omitted the Telegram alert, which is the one destination a visitor would
 * least expect.
 *
 * That accuracy is the point. A privacy policy describing a different website
 * is worse than none: it is a published, checkable false statement about how
 * personal data is handled.
 */
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { business } from '../data/business.ts';
---

<Legal
  title="Privacy Policy | Beyond Pixel Studio"
  h1="Privacy Policy"
  description="What Beyond Pixel Studio collects when you use this website, where it goes, how long it is kept, and how to have it removed."
  updated="2026-08-31"
>
  <p>
    This policy covers <strong>beyondpixel.studio</strong>. It describes what this
    website collects, where that information goes, and what you can ask us to do
    with it. It is written from how the site is actually built, not from a
    template.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect, and only when you send it</h2>
  <p>
    This site has no accounts, no logins and no comments. Nothing personal is
    collected by browsing it. Information reaches us only when you choose to
    send it, through one of three routes:
  </p>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Where</th><th>What it asks for</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Enquiry form (contact page)</td>
        <td>Name, phone number, email address, the service you are asking about, the event date if you give one, and your message</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Portfolio download</td>
        <td>Name, phone number, email address and the purpose of your enquiry, in exchange for the PDF</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>WhatsApp, phone and email links</td>
        <td>Whatever you write in the message you send. These open your own app — the message is not recorded by this website</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Where it goes</h2>
  <p>
    A submitted form is sent to a Google Apps Script belonging to us, which does
    two things with it:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      appends a row to a private Google Sheet in our own Google account, so we
      have a record of the enquiry; and
    </li>
    <li>
      sends the same details as a message to a private Telegram group used only
      by our team, so an enquiry is seen quickly rather than at the end of the
      day.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Both are internal. Your details are not sold, rented, published, or shared
    with anyone outside {business.name}, and we do not send marketing email to
    addresses collected here.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies and measurement</h2>
  <p>
    We set no cookies of our own. The site loads one third-party measurement
    tool:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Meta Pixel</strong> — records that a page was viewed and that an
      enquiry was submitted, so we can tell which advertising is working. It
      sets cookies belonging to Meta and is subject to
      <a href="https://www.facebook.com/privacy/policy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Meta's privacy policy</a>.
      It is not told your name, phone number or message.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Blocking it changes nothing about how the site works for you. Any browser
    setting, extension or tracking-protection feature that blocks it is welcome
    to.
  </p>

  <h2>Other services this site touches</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Hostinger</strong> hosts the site, on servers in Mumbai. Their
      systems keep ordinary web-server logs, including IP addresses.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>YouTube</strong> supplies the thumbnail images on the work pages,
      loaded from Google's servers. Video plays on YouTube, not here — nothing
      is embedded, so YouTube is not loaded until you click through.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Instagram</strong> is linked to. Clicking through leaves this
      site. No Instagram code runs on it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Google Fonts</strong> are not used. The typefaces are served from
      this site's own domain, so no font request goes to Google.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    Enquiries are kept while they are useful — an ongoing conversation, a
    booked job, or a record of work delivered — and reviewed periodically after
    that. Records connected to invoiced work are kept as long as Indian tax and
    company law requires. Enquiries that go nowhere are deleted on request, or
    when they are no longer of any use.
  </p>

  <h2>What you can ask for</h2>
  <p>
    Write to <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a> and you
    can ask us to:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>tell you what we hold about you;</li>
    <li>correct anything that is wrong;</li>
    <li>delete it, where we are not required to keep it; or</li>
    <li>stop contacting you.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We will respond within a reasonable period. Asking us to delete an enquiry
    does not remove messages you sent us on WhatsApp — those live in your own
    account as well as ours, and you can delete your copy yourself.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    This site is aimed at businesses and institutions and is not directed at
    children. We do not knowingly collect information from anyone under 18. If a
    parent or guardian believes we hold something we should not, write to us and
    it will be removed.
  </p>

  <h2>Security, stated plainly</h2>
  <p>
    The site is served over HTTPS, and the credentials that reach our Sheet and
    Telegram are held on Google's servers rather than in this website's code —
    the browser never holds them. That said, no method of transmission over the
    internet is completely secure, and we will not claim otherwise. Please do
    not send anything confidential through a web form.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes, the date at the top of the page changes with it.
  </p>
</Legal>
